Android: decide fseeko/ftello availability from the NDK API level.

The NDK CMake toolchain keeps CMAKE_SYSTEM_VERSION below 24 even for
ANDROID_PLATFORM=android-29, so 32-bit builds disabled fseeko and
include/share/compat.h then redefined it, clashing with bionic's stdio.h.
ANDROID_PLATFORM_LEVEL is the level the toolchain targets.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@
 endif()
 
 
-if(ANDROID AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_VERSION VERSION_LESS 24 AND (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "i686" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "armv7-a"))
+if(ANDROID AND ANDROID_PLATFORM_LEVEL VERSION_LESS 24 AND (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "i686" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "armv7-a"))
     # fseeko/ftello may link, but it's not usable before Android API 24 on 32-bit Android
     # https://android.googlesource.com/platform/bionic/+/main/docs/32-bit-abi.md
     message(STATUS "Disabling fseeko/ftello for 32-bit Android before API 24")
